# IDE
.idea/
.vs/
*.user

# Build output
bin/
obj/
artifacts/
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# Test / coverage output
TestResults/
*.trx
# ...but the Pester fixture is an input, not output: tools/tests/PortTools.Tests.ps1 reads it,
# so without this the tooling tests fail on every fresh clone and in CI.
!tools/tests/fixtures/*.trx
coverage*.xml
coverage*.json

# Python. tools/record-compile-corpus.py is run as a script, but anything that imports it - a
# probe, a REPL - drops bytecode next to it, which would then show up as a dirty tree and fail
# the slice driver's cleanliness check.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# Local-only
*.local.*
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/driver/

# The slice driver's own session log. Machine-local operational data, and gitignored on purpose:
# the budget gate counts slices from it, and `git clean -fd` during a failed-slice rollback would
# otherwise delete it and reset the driver's daily cap to zero. Measured tokens-per-slice get
# written into the slice's closing notes, which is where they belong for the record.
docs/plan/slice-log.jsonl

# Throwaway scratch for a working session: oracle scripts, build logs, TRX probes, one-off
# Python. Gitignored rather than banned, because the driver fails any slice whose working tree
# is dirty at the end and four forgotten scratch-*.py files at the repo root nearly threw away
# S08 (2026-08-30). Inside the repo so the sandboxed unattended session can actually write here,
# and ignored so a file left behind can never fail a slice. `git clean -fd` (no -x) leaves it
# alone, and `git stash push -u` does not pick it up.
.scratch/

# Session scaffolding for the human driving the port: the prompt handed to a fresh orchestrator
# session at the start of a phase. Untracked by choice - it describes how to run the work, not the
# work itself, and it goes stale the moment a phase ends. Gitignored rather than merely untracked
# because an unignored file at the repo root shows in `git status --porcelain`, which is exactly
# what the driver fails a slice for.
ORCHESTRATOR-PROMPT.md
.venvs/
